## Models shipped with Opera

UI element detector (assets/models/deki-yolo-int8.pte)
  deki-yolo by orasul (GNU General Public License v3.0),
  https://huggingface.co/orasul/deki-yolo, trained with Ultralytics YOLO.
  Converted to ExecuTorch and quantized to int8 for Opera.

Wake word model "Maestro" (public/wakeword/maestro.onnx, maestro_v3b)
  Trained with livekit-wakeword (Apache License 2.0),
    https://github.com/livekit/livekit-wakeword
  Audio front end: mel spectrogram from openWakeWord (Apache License 2.0
    repository), https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord
    Shipped as public/wakeword/melspectrogram_raw.onnx, modified for Opera:
    the graph stops before the final top_db clip.
  Speech embedding model: Google speech_embedding (Apache License 2.0),
    distributed through TensorFlow Hub and openWakeWord
    (public/wakeword/embedding_model.onnx, unmodified)
  Synthetic training speech: VoxCPM2 by OpenBMB (Apache License 2.0),
    https://huggingface.co/openbmb/VoxCPM2
  Negative and validation speech: FLEURS by Google (Creative Commons
    Attribution 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/),
    https://huggingface.co/datasets/google/fleurs. Audio was resampled and
    converted to speech embeddings, the audio is not redistributed.
  Background noise: MUSAN noise subset (public domain and Creative Commons
    Attribution 3.0 items), Snyder, Chen, Povey, "MUSAN: A Music, Speech,
    and Noise Corpus", arXiv:1510.08484
  Room impulse responses: OpenSLR RIRS_NOISES simulated RIRs (Apache
    License 2.0), https://www.openslr.org/28/

## Models downloaded by the user

Language, speech and voice models other than the ones above are not
distributed with Opera. They are downloaded on request from their publishers
(for example Hugging Face: Whisper by OpenAI, Supertonic by Supertone, LLMs)
and stay under the license chosen by their authors (Gemma Terms of Use,
Apache 2.0, MIT, OpenRAIL...). The user is responsible for accepting those
terms.
